text:
kevin_sales: quick heads-up  prospect (large payments org) wants streaming outputs as NDJSON lines, strict schema versioning, function/tool calls that produce machine-readable records, OIDC SSO, customer-managed KMS, and a 1-month pilot price. can eng/sec/ops confirm feasibility and an integration checklist? :wave:

anya_eng: clarifying q's before we scope: 1) inline function/tool results vs async callbacks? 2) do they require deterministic per-conversation ordering? 3) expected peak qps and tokens/day?

kevin_sales: inline for realtime risk decisions, async acceptable for batch enrichment. ordering is required for audit. estimate 55 qps peak, ~180k tokens/day during pilot.

anya_eng: implementation notes: we can stream NDJSON over SSE or websocket. SSE is simpler for client libraries, websocket gives bidirectional control (easier for cancellations). to guarantee ordering server-side use session affinity (sticky routing) so a conversation is pinned to a worker. we'll stamp each event with a schema_version field server-side so consumers can validate without guessing. minimal Node parsing pattern for SSE/NDJSON:```js
const es = new EventSource(url)
es.onmessage = e => {
  try {
    const obj = JSON.parse(e.data)
    // obj.schema_version -> pick schema validator
  } catch (err) {
    // handle partial chunk or malformed line
  }
}
```

rachel_sec: security constraints: OIDC or SAML supported. for CMK we support AWS KMS and GCP KMS for Dedicated/Private. Hosted CMK is available under enterprise contract. require SCIM for automated user provisioning and IP allowlist for admin endpoints. recommend short-lived API tokens + audit logs. for webhook callbacks we strongly advise mTLS and cert pinning for the buyer. on-prem HSMs will need enterprise track and add lead time.

tom_ops: ops notes: to preserve strict ordering pick Dedicated capacity with session pinning. if they must stay hosted we can approximate ordering but risk cross-worker reordering under heavy burst. enable per-token cost visibility in Console and export traces to their SIEM. for NDJSON ingestion we recommend clients implement backpressure and line-buffered parsing; we also support an event type for "function_result" so async jobs are easier to reconcile.

kevin_sales: procurement asked for a quick ballpark: 1 month pilot, 180k tokens/day streaming + function calls. what numbers can we give?

anya_eng: rough hosted estimate: streaming generation ~ $0.00072 per token (model-dependent example). 180k/day * 30 = 5.4M tokens -> ~$3.9k/mo. if they need ordering SLA and pinned throughput use Dedicated reserved capacity  expect an initial monthly commit in the low-to-mid $20k range depending on instance family/region. can run a model-mix sim to tighten numbers.

rachel_sec: timeline for security review: standard SAQ + OIDC + KMS integration ~2 weeks. add 1-2 weeks for SCIM provisioning and mTLS webhook testing. on-prem HSMs add substantial lead time.

tom_ops: ops followups: we will queue a Dedicated sizing job if they sign. also propose an auto-fallback policy: on high load degrade to a quantized INT8 variant or smaller context model. typical policy is failover at >=95th percentile latency or when queue depth exceeds threshold. this lowers cost and maintains availability.

kevin_sales: can we get a short checklist I can send to the buyer and a tiny sample NDJSON line to include in the SAQ response?

anya_eng: compact integration checklist for customer: 1) pick model(s) and token budget for pilot 2) choose hosting mode (Hosted / Dedicated / Private) 3) select SSO type (OIDC/SAML) + SCIM for provisioning 4) select KMS type (AWS KMS / GCP KMS / Redwood-managed) 5) decide sync vs async function flows and provide webhook endpoints with mTLS if used 6) provide JSON schema(s) and versioning plan (we will stamp schema_version) 7) telemetry destination (SIEM) and retention policy 8) pilot timeline and success criteria (throughput / p99 latency / correctness)

anya_eng: sample NDJSON line (one line per event):
{"event":"function_call","schema_version":"v2","function":"assess_risk","arguments":{"tx_id":"txn_9f3b","amount":542.75,"currency":"USD"}}

provision-bot: [task] queued pool-sizing job id ps-5599  action required only after purchase order.

rachel_sec: i'll attach typical SAQ answers and a short note on required test accounts + SCIM test user list. also will include checklist of certs for webhook mTLS.

tom_ops: i'll draft a short fallback & backpressure runbook (NDJSON client patterns, reconnection jitter) and an ops playbook for Dedicated pool scaling.

kevin_sales: awesome  i'll send this to buyer with SAQ and ask for NDA to share Private deployment architecture. anya, can you run the model-mix sim with a quantized option and post numbers tomorrow?

anya_eng: yes  i'll run simulator and include cost/latency tradeoffs for full vs INT8 quantized variants and a suggested fallback rule set. will post by EOD tomorrow. :+1:
